  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the claim direction. For H24 (TP53 loss versus intact, direction +1, dependency_USP7), discovery was +0.396 (95% CI +0.325 to +0.467) and independent validation was +0.437 (independent interval +0.336 to +0.537). This is a very large effect on the dependency_USP7 scale and is bounded away from zero after independent validation. I therefore accept H24 as a robust dataset-specific association and close it: TP53 loss is associated with weaker/less-negative USP7 dependency in this dataset. This is not a causal or external-generalizability claim. For H42 (adherent-culture modification of the MSI-high/WRN effect, direction -1), discovery gave +0.105 (95% CI +0.037 to +0.172), but independent validation gave -0.011 (independent interval -0.121 to +0.099). The validation point is essentially null and opposite in sign, and the independent interval does not support a stable positive adherent-culture interaction. I reject H42 as a supported context-specific refinement, while noting that its validation interval is not an equivalence proof against every possible small or opposite interaction. This rejection does not undermine the overall MSI-high/WRN claim: H7 remains robustly accepted with discovery +0.790 (95% CI +0.760 to +0.819) and independent validation +0.822 (independent interval +0.776 to +0.868). Given the validated main effect and the failed culture interaction, I close H7. I also close the main H11 association because PTEN-loss/STAT3 was validated (+0.309, independent interval +0.232 to +0.386). However, H40 remains active because its discovery library interaction is still potentially important; the registered simple-effect analyses in Avana and non-Avana library contexts (H51 and H52) are the appropriate next refinement. Current robust dataset-specific associations are H6, H7, H11, H17, and H24, with H6 and H17 now the highest-priority unvalidated accepted effects. The next best analyses are H50-H52: check whether WRN/MSI-high remains strong within adherent culture, and decompose the PTEN-loss/STAT3 library-context signal. After those, validation should target H6 first, then H17. These conclusions describe associations in the supplied data, not causality or generalizable biology.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 4 synthesis update. Robust accepted dataset-specific main associations: H6 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency (large discovery, unvalidated; priority 1 validation); H7 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency (validated; closed after H42 culture interaction failed validation); H11 PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency (validated; main closed, but context H40 remains active); H17 KEAP1 loss -> weaker/less-negative NFE2L2 dependency (large discovery, unvalidated; priority 2 validation); H24 TP53 loss -> weaker/less-negative USP7 dependency (validated; closed). H42 adherent-culture interaction for WRN failed independent validation: discovery +0.105 CI +0.037 to +0.172, validation -0.011 independent interval -0.121 to +0.099; reject as meaningful positive interaction. This supports treating H7 as an overall effect rather than an adherent-specific effect in this dataset, though the validation interval is not formal equivalence. H40 PTEN-loss/STAT3 by Avana library remains unresolved/active: discovery interaction +0.196 CI +0.033 to +0.358, but non-Avana PTEN-loss cell is small and independent library validation not yet available. Registered refinements H51/H52 will estimate the PTEN-loss/STAT3 simple effects by library; H50 estimates the adherent WRN/MSI-high simple effect. Next analysis should prioritize H50-H52. Next validation priority after those should be H6, then H17. Deferred unresolved main claims remain H1, H4, H8, H9. No causal or external-generalizability claims are supported."
